    {
      "id": "1.3.1",
      "title": "Integrate staged-ending provenance and relocation into current-source edit/seen recovery",
      "status": "done",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-05T12:54:44.072Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-11-05T13:26:57.431Z",
      "startedAt": "2026-11-05T13:20:30.994Z",
      "report": {
        "outcome": "Integrated staged-line provenance and relocation, then wired exact current-source observation into the public batch path. Drift authorizes in the model's original coordinates, relocates through unique anchor windows, refuses absent/ambiguous targets and REM, returns bounded current tagged context, and carries authored plus delivered seen intervals into the post-commit snapshot. Live drift integration passes.",
        "decisions": [
          "Relocation lives in PlanBatch after block/register resolution — unresolved syntax blocks cannot be relocated correctly.",
          "Drift drops prior seen mapping except authored lines — we have no diff-level provenance yet; this is fail-safe, not full donor seen remapping."
        ],
        "open": [
          "Diff-based seen remapping of unchanged lines across external drift is not implemented; only authored lines and delivered post-edit views are carried."
        ]
      },
      "endedAt": "2026-11-05T13:26:57.431Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "1.3.2",
      "title": "Integrate secret payload guards after captured-shape and detector-gap fixes",
      "status": "done",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-05T12:54:44.072Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-11-05T13:29:52.127Z",
      "startedAt": "2026-11-05T13:27:01.632Z",
      "report": {
        "outcome": "Integrated the fail-closed payload guard engine and fixed the known placeholder-embedding fail-open: larger credentials containing or overlapping canonical markers are now redacted as a whole, while only shorter values wholly inside a marker stay shielded. Race tests pass for the full secrets package.",
        "decisions": [
          "Integrate the guard engine but do not yet enable a provider/tool secret boundary — host wiring and real captured payload coverage belong to Phase I."
        ],
        "open": [
          "Guard shapes are still partly derived from declared host structs rather than captured live provider requests; wiring the general boundary before capture would be dishonest."
        ]
      },
      "endedAt": "2026-11-05T13:29:52.127Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "1.3.3",
