        "outcome": "Committed c6dc366: Secrets.toml is now a real layer (agent + trusted project) whose secrets.patterns/exclusions append across layers, with origin enforcement in both directions, actionable malformed diagnostics naming file and line, last-valid retention, trust gating and Save refusal. Unknown-key preservation, cross-process concurrent saves and denied trust widening were already covered by existing tests; just check passes.",
        "decisions": [
          "Model Secrets.toml as a second document per scope with append semantics rather than a new Scope enum — keeps compose and Save semantics intact.",
          "Restrict the settings command to Workbench.toml and refuse detection-policy edits with a message naming Secrets.toml instead of silently writing the wrong file.",
          "Mark the two keys pending: validation and layering are real, the detector consumer arrives in Phase I."
        ],
